WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.652
This simple record illustrates representation cleaning.

00:00:02.652 --> 00:00:07.342
The name changes spacing and display case.

00:00:07.342 --> 00:00:09.192
The email is trimmed and lowercased.

00:00:09.192 --> 00:00:11.282
The phone keeps only digits.

00:00:11.282 --> 00:00:16.317
Each transformation is explainable. But the cleaned value should not erase the source evidence.

00:00:16.317 --> 00:00:20.952
In many analytical workflows, raw and cleaned layers are both valuable.

00:00:20.952 --> 00:00:28.062
Connect this idea to a product catalog standardizing categories and quarantining invalid rows.

00:00:28.062 --> 00:00:33.097
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:33.097 --> 00:00:41.142
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:41.142 --> 00:00:45.922
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:45.922 --> 00:00:50.800
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
